-- title:
--   Uniform bound for twisted orbital integrals of a double coset
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ Galois, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every element of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$ (so the group is cyclic with generator $\sigma$). Fix a nonzero prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $E_v = L \otimes_K K_v$ for $K_v$ the $v$-adic completion, and fix $a \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$. The assertion is the existence of a constant $C \ge 0$, depending on all of these data including $a$, with the following property. Let $\delta \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$ have vanishing $(1,0)$ and $(0,1)$ entries, and suppose that the $K_v$-algebra norms (taken on $E_v$) of its two diagonal entries $\delta_{00}$ and $\delta_{11}$ are distinct. Let $\tau'$ be a measure, for the Borel $\sigma$-algebra, on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser $\{t : t\delta\,\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\}$ of $\delta$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$ (with $\sigma$ acting through the induced automorphism of $\mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$), assume $\tau'$ is a Haar measure, and assume it gives mass $1$ to the part of that subgroup lying in the semi-local integral set $\mathcal{K}_v$, i.e. the set of $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$ such that all entries of both $g$ and $g^{-1}$ lie in the image of $\mathcal{O}_L \otimes \mathcal{O}_{K_v}$ in $E_v$. Finally, let $I \in \mathbb{C}$ be a twisted orbital integral of the indicator function, with value $1$, of the double coset $\mathcal{K}_v\,a\,\mathcal{K}_v$ at $\delta$ against $\tau'$: that is, there is a weight function $w$ satisfying the project's twisted section condition for $(\sigma, \delta, \tau')$ and that function such that $I = \int \mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{K}_v a \mathcal{K}_v}(x^{-1}\delta\,\sigma(x))\, w(x)\,\mathrm{d}\mu$, with $\mu$ the semi-local Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(E_v)$ normalised by the integral compacts. Then $$\|N(\delta_{00}) - N(\delta_{11})\|\cdot\|I\| \le C\,\|N(\delta_{00})N(\delta_{11})\|^{1/2},$$ the exponent being a real power.
--
--   This is the uniform local boundedness estimate for twisted orbital integrals of the characteristic function of a general semi-local double coset $\mathcal{K}_v a \mathcal{K}_v$, evaluated at diagonal elements whose diagonal entries have distinct norms; the bound is of Harish-Chandra type, with the logarithmic factors of the sharper estimate absorbed into the constant. It feeds the corresponding statement for arbitrary semi-local test functions, obtained by covering such a test function by finitely many double cosets.
